  "query_preview": "..\nCurrent satellite imagery shows increasing cloud cover and radar\nshows some light returns entering western Pima County. As the \nbetter forcing and associated cold front arrives later today, \nisolated to scattered showers will be possible. Best chance \ncontinues to be north of the area, favoring Pinal and northern \nGraham/Greenlee Cos. A rumble of thunder will be possible as\nwell, but will also favor further north where better dynamics\nexist. Outside of the rain chances, breezy S/SW winds are also\nexpected today with speeds of 15-20 mph and gusts up to 30 mph.\nRain chances quickly end from west to east by evening. \n\nThereafter, the upper level pattern will become zonal after the\ntrough exits the region this evening and early Wednesday. This \nperiod will generally be benign and dry until the next weather \nsystem coming though on Friday. This second system will nearly \nfollow the previous weather system, but it will be even more dry\nwith some breezes.\n\nTemperatures will follow the roller coaster of below normal to \nslight above normal for the week due to the passing weather \nsystems. Long range ensemble models show another period of \ntroughiness late weekend to early next week, potentially leading\nto a chance for rain showers and breezes.",
